#7 Hook declarations -- CORRECTED. The premise does not hold for these ranges.
   app.rs's single declare_hooks! is at :9187 (the brief said :9185).
   No moved body reads a QUANTICK_* at all. Every std::env::var of an
   app.rs-declared hook is in new_with_workspace -- QUANTICK_CONTROL_EVIDENCE
   at app.rs:825 -- or in harness.rs; the moved regions name QUANTICK_* only
   in doc comments and log messages, which crates/guards/src/generated.rs
   (literal_hook_names, which cuts the // tail) does not count as a read.
   So no declaration moves, hooks::OWNERS is untouched, and the generated
   registry stays byte-identical -- which is what the brief wanted. Had a
   declaration moved, it could not have: the registry's 'Declared in' column
   is fused from OWNERS at crates/app/src/hooks.rs:337, so moving one
   rewrites that cell. See GOAL.md S6.

